# Authoritative documentation map

This project carries a copy of the framework manuals under `docs/` (generated by `papa new`). That copy can lag the framework — **when a Papa checkout is available, its `papa/docs/` is the authority**. The paths below are framework-checkout paths; the same manual usually exists in this project as `docs/<name>.md`.

For what changed between framework versions — removed APIs, new config keys, behavior changes you must account for before upgrading — read `papa/docs/issues/changes.md`. It is **not** copied into generated projects, so it only exists in the checkout.

| Need | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Orientation and current feature set | `papa/docs/README.md` |
| Fetcher contracts, tasks, fetching, errors, stage design | `papa/docs/FETCHER_WRITING_GUIDE.md` |
| YAML scope, validation, migration, durations, runtime behavior | `papa/docs/CORE_CONFIG.md` |
| Task JSON versus independent business tables | `papa/docs/DATA_LANDING_GUIDE.md` |
| Monitor auth, APIs, tables, actions, pages, operation logs | `papa/docs/MONITOR.md` |
| Commands for scaffolding, HTML/Rod evidence, selectors, checks | `papa/docs/CLI.md` |
| Build, tests, race checks, Windows shell notes | `papa/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` |
| Runtime observability: event contract, `obs` config, `papa report` artifacts, business extensions | `papa/docs/OBSERVABILITY.md` |
| Failed task reprocessing | `papa/docs/ERROR_QUEUE.md` |
| Startup recovery of pending/processing tasks | `papa/docs/RECOVER_QUEUE.md` |
| Per-task periodic polling | `papa/docs/REPEAT_QUEUE.md` |
| Why generic cron was removed | `papa/docs/issues/SCHEDULER_REDESIGN.md` |
| What changed between framework versions (read before upgrading) | `papa/docs/issues/changes.md` |
| Oao declarations and component boundary | `oao/README.md` |

## Conflict rules

- The active exported API and tests outrank prose.
- `papa/docs/` outranks `crawler/docs/` when the latter is a generated copy.
- Do not copy a `scheduler:` block or recommend `RegisterCronJob`; current Papa removed generic cron. Use repeatable tasks for interval polling and a business-owned scheduler for wall-clock jobs.
- Strict YAML validation rejects unknown keys. Never retain a legacy key merely because an old generated configuration contains it.
- When comments in the business project disagree with current manuals, fix or flag the comments rather than teaching the old behavior.

## Efficient reading

Do not load all manuals for every request. Start with README plus the primary manual from the table, then follow links only when the task crosses boundaries. Search source for exact public symbols before writing code.
